#: Game.Levels.PfWorld
msgid "# **Proof Strategy World**\n"
"So far, we've really only attempted so-called **direct proofs**. This is where our goal is of the form §0 so we make §1 an **Assumption** (using the §2 tactic) and then our goal becomes §3.\n"
"\n"
"But there are many other proof strategies that can be more appropriate (given the situation) and easier to manage. In Lean, these proof strategies are realized through various **tactics** -- for example, §4 is the tactic we use for a direct proof strategy. In this world, we'll learn about tactics that help implement the following proof strategies:\n"
"* **Indirect proofs:** proofs by contraposition, proofs by contradiction\n"
"* **Proofs involving quantifiers:** universally and existentially quantified statements\n"
"* **Proofs of conjunctions**: proofs of §5 and §6 statements\n"
"* **Proofs involving disjunctions:** proofs of §7 statements, proof by cases\n"
"* **Existence and uniqueness proofs: proofs involving the quantifier §8\n"
">\n"
"We'll mostly learn by example here, but we'll justify our proof strategies along the way too. Let's get started!"
