#: Game.Levels.ArgWorld.L02_arg
msgid "# **Level 2**\n"
"This valid argument is sometimes referred to as **Modus Tolens**. Of course, we can prove that Modus Tolens is valid by staring at the truth-table serving as the graphic for this world! But let's try to prove it in Lean. To do so, there's a logical equivalence from worlds of yore that will make this problem look more like the last one..."
msgstr ""

#: Game.Levels.QuantifierWorld.L06_quant
msgid "Negated Existential"
msgstr ""

#: Game.Levels.SetWorld
msgid "Set World"
msgstr ""

#. §0: `by_contra`
#. §1: `⊢ P`
#. §2: `⊢ False`
#. §3: `this : ¬ P`
#. §4: `this`
#. §5: `by_contra F`
#. §6: `⊢ False`
#. §7: `F : ¬ P`
#: Game.Levels.PfWorld.pf_docs
msgid "The tactic §0 changes a goal of the form §1 to §2 and adds the hypothesis §3 to the proof-state. One can name the introduced hypothesis §4 with an optional identifier. For example, §5 changes the goal to §6 and adds the hypothesis §7."
msgstr ""

#: Game.Levels.SetWorld.SetWorld_eg.L06_set
#: Game.Levels.PfWorld.PfWorld_eg.L06_pf
msgid "### **Level 6**"
msgstr ""

#: Game.Levels.QuantifierWorld.QuantifierWorld_eg
msgid "Quantifier World Examples"
msgstr ""

#. §0: `P`
#. §1: `Q`
#. §2: `P`
#. §3: `Q`
#. §4: `P`
#: Game.Levels.EquivWorld.EquivWorld_eg.L05_equiv
msgid "The statement *§0 implies §1* is logically equivalent to *§2 and §3, or not §4*."
msgstr ""

#: Game.Levels.EquivWorld.L02_equiv
msgid "The **contrapositive** of an implication is logically equivalent to the original implication."
msgstr ""

#: Game.Levels.ArgWorld.L05_arg
msgid "This valid argument is known as *Conjunctive Amplification*."
msgstr ""

#: Game.Levels.SetWorld.L11_set
msgid "Super. We now need to prove this logical equivalence. We might start by rewriting what it means to be a member of an intersection..."
msgstr ""

#. §0: `∧`
#. §1: $$ (P ∧ Q) ∧ R ↔ P ∧ (Q ∧ R) $$
#. §2: `And_assoc`
#. §3: $$
#. \\begin{array}{|ccc||cc|}
#.   \\hline
#.   P & Q & R & (P ∧ Q) ∧ R & P ∧ (Q ∧ R) \\
#.   \\hline
#.   T & T & T & T & T \\
#.   T & T & F & F & F \\
#.   T & F & T & F & F \\
#.   T & F & F & F & F \\
#.   F & T & T & F & F \\
#.   F & T & F & F & F \\
#.   F & F & T & F & F \\
#.   F & F & F & F & F \\
#.   \\hline
#. \\end{array}
#. $$
#: Game.Levels.EquivWorld.equiv_docs
msgid "This is the **Associative Law** for §0. It says that\n"
"\n"
"§1\n"
"\n"
"The proof of §2 is given in the truth-table below:\n"
"§3"
msgstr ""

#. §0: `A : I → Set u`
#. §1: `A`
#. §2: `I`
#. §3: `Set u`
#. §4: `u`
#. §5: `A`
#. §6: `I = {1,2,3}`
#. §7: ```
#. ⋂ i, A i = { x | ∀ i, x ∈ A i}
#. ```
#: Game.Levels.SetWorld.L10_set
msgid "# **Level 10: Unions of Indexed Families**\n"
"| | | |\n"
"|---|:---:|---|\n"
"| | ![Venn diagram of intersection of an indexed family](images/venn_iinter.png) | |\n"
">\n"
"Let §0. This means that §1 is a function from §2 (an indexing set) to §3, sets in the universe §4. Or as we say in class, an **indexed** family of sets. The intersection of all members of §5 (illustrated above where §6) is defined by:\n"
"§7\n"
"But, as before, first and foremost our goal is a subset relation which we know is really just a universally quantified goal. Let's begin by introducing the appropriate stuff..."
msgstr ""

#. §0: `A B : Set u`
#. §1: `∩`
#. §2: ```
#. A ∩ B = {x | x ∈ A ∧ x ∈ B}
#. ```
#. §3: `x ∈ A ∩ B`
#. §4: `x ∈ A ∧ x ∈ B`
#. §5: `x ∈ A ∩ B`
#. §6: `x ∈ A ∧ x ∈ B`
#. §7: ```
#. rw[mem_inter_iff] at h
#. ```
#: Game.Levels.SetWorld.L03_set
msgid "# **Level 3: Intersections**\n"
"| | | |\n"
"|---|:---:|---|\n"
"| | ![Venn diagram of intersection connective](images/venn_inter.png) | |\n"
">\n"
"If §0 then the set connective §1 (intersection), illustrated above, is defined as follows:\n"
"§2\n"
"This means that, definitionally, to say that §3 means the same thing as §4. 👉 To rewrite §5 as §6 use\n"
"§7"
